= The Eighth Party Congress, Leipzig

The party meets in Leipzig, from the end of January into the first days of February. Heinrich Brandler's Zentrale has the majority and a plan: the united front, the demand for a workers' government, and patient work in the unions and factory councils. In the corridors, Ruth Fischer and Arkadi Maslow speak for a Left that thinks the party is waiting on the SPD leaders for a revolution that those leaders will never carry out.

Both sides have an argument, and the congress has to give one of them the floor.

- @confirm: Confirm Brandler's Zentrale and the united front.
- @balance: Offer the Left two seats in the Zentrale.
- @leftturn: Give the Left the floor and move the party toward offensive action.

@confirm
subtitle: Right +4 strength, Left +6 dissent. Zentrale: 21 members, Left 0. Zentralausschuss: Left about a third. · dev: kf_right_strength +4, kf_left_dissent +6, trust +3
on-arrival: kf_right_strength += 4; kf_left_dissent += 6; comintern_trust += 3; zentrale_n = 21; zentrale_l = 0; za_n = 38; za_l = 13
go-to: root

The congress confirms the Zentrale by a clear majority and enlarges it from fourteen members to twenty-one. The majority will not seat Fischer's people. On Radek's proposal it elects three moderate leftists instead, Ewert, Lindau and Pfeiffer, none of whom the Left counts as its own. The united front line is the party's policy, and the Left is outvoted, which in this party means it will wait for its chance rather than change its mind.

@balance
subtitle: Left +3 strength, Right +3 dissent. Zentrale: 21 members, Left 2. Zentralausschuss: Left a strong minority. · dev: kf_left_strength +3, kf_right_dissent +3
on-arrival: kf_left_strength += 3; kf_right_dissent += 3; zentrale_n = 21; zentrale_l = 2; za_n = 38; za_l = 16
go-to: root

Two Left delegates are admitted to the enlarged Zentrale. The Right calls it an invitation to sabotage and the Left calls it a token. Only Zetkin, who wanted peace above all, is pleased.

@leftturn
subtitle: Left +6 strength, Right +10 dissent, Moscow unimpressed. Zentrale: 21 members, Left 6. Zentralausschuss: Left the majority. · dev: kf_left_strength +6, kf_right_dissent +10, trust −4, y23_hundreds +1
on-arrival: kf_left_strength += 6; kf_right_dissent += 10; comintern_trust -= 4; y23_hundreds += 1; zentrale_n = 21; zentrale_l = 6; za_n = 38; za_l = 20
go-to: root

The congress adopts resolutions on armed workers' units that would be at home in a more revolutionary year. The Right is furious, and Moscow, whose line at this moment is the workers' government, reads it as indiscipline.
